  message: "FOLDED 2026-09-06 into INV-bikaj-mizug-gahoh-mofij-pigut-funaj-zijab-rivil as its named instance, by owner ruling on INV-nanon's re-scope (walk-through item 4). Same defect, one pass: a framework linker that runs with its patterns absent. Status unchanged (invariants have no wont_do); the duplicate_of link removes it from `ready`. The fix lands under INV-bikaj via INV-hujog's declaration mechanism."  # d5d2
- op: discuss  # bec1
  at: '2026-09-16T19:27:04Z'  # bec1
  by: agent  # bec1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # bec1
  clock: 10  # bec1
  nonce: bec1  # bec1
  message: "RE-MEASURED AT TIP 2026-09-16 (dev db846f196f), AND THIS ITEM'S FILED\nroot_cause IS WRONG. Not stale -- wrong, since May.\n\nTHE FALSE PREMISE. root_cause reads: \"files_analyzed=0 suggests it's reading the\nin-memory IR but finding no DI patterns\". It is not reading the in-memory IR.\nlink_di_resolution calls extract_bindings_from_source(ctx.repo_root), which\niterates find_non_test_files(root, _SOURCE_GLOBS) and calls read_masked_source\non every .java/.kt/.scala/.cs/.ts/.tsx/.py file, plus _scan_spi_files over\nMETA-INF/services. MEASURED by attributing Path.read_text/read_bytes to the\ncalling linker on a full self-survey: di-resolution-linker READ 396 FILES. The\nzero was a missing counter, not a measurement -- the pass never assigned\nrun.files_analyzed.\n\nCONSEQUENCE, which is worse than the cost this item was filed for: because\nfiles_analyzed was 0, derive_silence_reason stamped di-resolution\nsilence_reason='no_candidate_files', a value documented as \"the pass received\nzero input files ... the only silence the orchestrator can attribute with\ncertainty\". The provenance record asserted, with certainty, something false\nabout this pass. That is the second half of INV-nanon's statement (\"the\nprovenance record should report the pass as skipped with a documented reason\")\nproducing a wrong reason for the very pass INV-nanon named as its instance.\n\nFIXED IN PR #1005. files_analyzed is now derived from a per-invocation read log\nbound at the linker chokepoint. di-resolution at tip reports 396 files and\nsilence_reason='unreported' -- cannot-determine, the honest residue. It joins\nthe 11-run cohort that WI-finij owns.\n\nTHE COST HALF, re-measured, still standing but much smaller than filed:\n  filed 2026-05-28   2550 ms  (2.7% of total pass time)\n  2026-07-30         3394 ms\n  2026-09-16 tip      988 ms  (0.48% of 207647 ms)\nA 2.6x absolute drop and a 5.6x share drop since filing, with no work done on\nthis pass -- the denominator grew and the pass got cheaper.\n\nTHE ASK IS STILL NOT DONE. The item asks the pass to \"short-circuit on absence\nof DI markers\". It does not, and the reason is now precise rather than\nspeculative: di-resolution-linker declares activation=LinkerActivation(always=True)\nEXPLICITLY -- one of only 12 linkers that deliberately opt into running\nunconditionally, as against 25 that inherit always=True by silent default. So\nthis is a decision somebody made, not an omission. Changing it to\nframeworks=[...] is the WITHHOLDING direction (a missed framework detection\nsilently drops real edges), so it is surfaced for the owner on INV-nanon with\nthe census, not performed here.\n\nStatus unchanged (violated; folded into INV-bikaj by the 2026-09-06 owner\nruling, and invariants have no wont_do). The root_cause field is corrected\nbelow."  # bec1
- op: update  # acc7
